{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development results in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. Furthermore, the applicant fails to&nbsp; demonstrate that the home will be provided for children and young people who meet this threshold i.e. being a&nbsp;specialist and can demonstrate experience of managing complex young people and those with disabilities,&nbsp;thus would not meet the current needs of LBBD Children’s Social Care, as confirmed by LBBD&#39;s Lead Commissioner in Children&#39;s Social Care.&nbsp; As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp; - National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024);-&nbsp;Policies D7, H1, H12 and S2 of the London Plan (March 2021); and-&nbsp;Policies SP3 and&nbsp;SPDG1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)"
  ],
